# nvm-manager – Architecture Overview

## Monorepo Structure

```
apps/api/   – Express 5 REST API   (Node ≥ 22, TS 6; port 3789, bind: 127.0.0.1)
apps/web/   – Angular 22 SPA        (zoneless; port 4200, proxies /api → 3789)
apps/e2e/   – Playwright E2E tests
```

## Key Decisions

**nvm is a shell function, not a binary.**
The backend therefore spawns a `bash -c` subshell for every nvm call,
sources `nvm.sh`, and executes the command (`apps/api/src/nvm/nvm.service.ts`).

**Bind to 127.0.0.1 only – never 0.0.0.0.**
The backend executes shell commands; network exposure would be a security risk.

**No database.**
nvm itself (filesystem under `~/.nvm`) is the single source of truth.
The API queries nvm live on every request.

**Angular Signals instead of NgRx.**
The app-wide state is manageable (active version, log, modal, loading flags).
Signals + computed() are fully sufficient without an external state management library.
Server reads use `httpResource()` (signal-backed GET); mutations use a thin `HttpClient`
service; validated inputs use Signal Forms (`@angular/forms/signals`). All stable in v22.

**`nvm use` → internally `nvm alias default`.**
`nvm use` only changes the version for the current shell process (lost immediately).
`nvm alias default` writes persistently to `~/.nvm/alias/default`.

**Two-layered shell injection protection:**
1. Whitelist regex validators in `nvm.types.ts` (before the call)
2. Single-quote escaping in `nvm.service.ts` (at call time)

